{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-moduli-symmetry-d4-novelty","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:moduli-symmetry-d4-novelty","kind":"remark","title":"Mathematical novelty of $\\mathbb{Z}[i]$ as ring of definition for the Möbius family","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-moduli-symmetry-d4"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-moduli-symmetry-d4","text":"moduli-symmetry-d4-novelty.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:moduli-symmetry-d4-novelty\"></a><p><strong>Remark.</strong> To lock the moduli line symmetries to a complex algebraic origin, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{Z}[i]</code> rather than <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{Z}</code> serves as the ring of definition for the Möbius family under the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">D_4</code> action.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/moduli-symmetry-d4-novelty.md","heading":"Remark","number":"15.19.8"}
